Changes made to the original (see also the header of hooks/holdpane.mjs):
- a second hook for the PowerShell tool, and one for the Monitor tool;
- reading PowerShell, cmd.exe and nested shell commands, not only Bash;
- looking up Git's bash, find, du and sleep on Windows instead of assuming them on PATH;
- measuring PowerShell deletions natively, without following junctions or symbolic links;
- refusing the command when the mod itself fails (a .catch on every hook);
- measuring that only reads: no project tools are run before the user has answered;
- a command line reader that handles quotes, comments, heredocs and here-strings.

